From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cli: reject command errors as unavailable topology

libemcli represents a command transport failure as a valid JSON status tree.
The topology handler checked only for a nil tree, so it traversed the status
object as topology and returned HTTP 200 with empty nodes and edges.  A
temporary controller failure therefore looked exactly like authoritative
proof that the entire mesh had disappeared.

Require the Device root before constructing a topology response and use HTTP
503 for either missing command data or a status/error tree.  This lets the
browser and experiment harness distinguish observation failure from a real
empty network.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/rdkb-cli/main.go | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
--- a/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
+++ b/src/rdkb-cli/main.go
@@ -4247,12 +4247,16 @@ func loadTopologyFromDeviceTree(w  http.ResponseWriter) {
 
     topologyTree := execEMCommand(cmd, nil)
     if topologyTree == nil {
-        http.Error(w, "Failed to fetch reset tree", http.StatusInternalServerError)
+        http.Error(w, "Controller topology unavailable", http.StatusServiceUnavailable)
         return
     }
     defer C.free_network_tree(topologyTree)
 
     topoDeviceTree := getNetworkTreeByKey(topologyTree, "Device")
+    if topoDeviceTree == nil {
+        http.Error(w, "Controller topology unavailable", http.StatusServiceUnavailable)
+        return
+    }
 
     // Helper to create STA list with circular layout
     createSTAList := func(deviceX, deviceY float32, radioList []Radio) []map[string]interface{} {
